# SynthLink board font overrides — tier 0 of the font decision.
#
# A handful of boards are not drawn against CP437. An Amiga board's art is cut
# against Topaz and its high bytes are ISO-8859-1, so read as CP437 it comes out
# as a hail of guillemets and fractions. This file says which boards get which
# font, and the font carries everything else: a registry entry names the
# typeface, the encoding it is drawn against, and the column count it implies,
# so ONE id here settles all three. SyncTERM makes the same choice and says so
# in its manual — a font is chosen "and by implication, a codepage".
#
# It is not a preference. A board listed here is served its font whatever the
# user last picked with the Aa button, which is why the button says so and goes
# inert for the duration of the call. Nothing is written to the user's stored
# font: hang up and their own choice is back.
#
# Format, one per line:
#   host:port  fontid     that board, that port
#   host       fontid     every port on that host
#   # comment             ignored, as are blank lines
#
# Hostnames are matched case-insensitively; a host:port line wins over a bare
# host line. An id no font answers to is ignored, with a line in the log — a
# typo leaves the board on the user's own font rather than on no font at all.
#
# Edits are live on the next /altfonts.json request (this file's mtime is
# checked), the same as config/curated.txt and config/blacklist.txt. Nothing to
# restart.
#
# The ids are in public/fonts/index.js. Today there is exactly one that is not
# CP437:
#
#   topaz1200    Amiga Topaz 2+, ISO-8859-1, 80 columns

# aBSiNTHE BBS is the board this was built for — CNet PRO on Amiga hardware.
# Its address is NOT filled in here because this checkout has never had it: it
# is not in curated.txt and nothing in the repo names it. Put the real
# host:port on the line below and it goes live on the next request.
#
# aBSiNTHE BBS
# <host>:<port>   topaz1200
absinthebbs.net:1940 topaz1200
